CONTACT;X-BEDEWORK-UID=00f1fcdb-0f068baf-010f-068baf83-00000004:None
CREATED:20260427T172414Z
DESCRIPTION:The Duke Department of Music invites you to our first Biddle C
 ommunity Day!\n\nJoin us as we open our doors and welcome the broader Tri
 angle and on-campus communities to experience the sounds\, activities\, a
 nd vibrant life of the Biddle Music Building. From live performances and 
 open rehearsals to interactive activities-including bucket bands\, sheet 
 music origami\, painting to music\, karaoke\, and informal conversations-
 guests of all ages are invited to explore the creativity and energy that 
 define Duke Music.\n\nCome and go throughout the day\, meet our students 
 and faculty\, and experience music as it is created\, explored\, and shar
 ed. Then continue the evening at our Faculty and Student Gala\, taking pl
 ace next door in Baldwin Auditorium beginning at 7:30 PM.\n\nWe look forw
 ard to seeing you!\n\nMore details are visible at https://music.duke.edu/
 biddle-community-day.\n\nThis event is part of "We the People\," a Duke a
 nd Durham collaboration marking the 250th anniversary of the signing of t
 he Declaration of Independence through public events that examine the nat
 ion's evolving identity. Drawing from the opening words of the Constituti
 on\, the project invites us to consider who "the people" have been and wh
 o we aspire to be within the ongoing story of the United States.
DURATION:PT10H30M
