CREATED:20260714T171502Z
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the artistry\, mentorship\, and community at the hea
 rt of Duke Music during the 2026 Faculty & Student Gala Concert. This all
 -Mendelssohn program brings together distinguished faculty\, accomplished
  alumni\, and exceptional student musicians in honor of the retirement of
  renowned Mendelssohn scholar Dr. R. Larry Todd.\n\nThe program opens wit
 h the Duke Symphony Orchestra\, conducted by Harry Davidson\, performing 
 the atmospheric Hebrides Overture\, inspired by the dramatic Scottish lan
 dscape of Fingal's Cave. Next\, pianist Bryan Tong joins the orchestra in
  a rare performance of Mendelssohn's unfinished Piano Concerto No. 3 in E
  Minor\, meticulously reconstructed with the extraordinary musical schola
 rship and creativity of Dr. Todd.  \n\nThe evening culminates with the Ci
 ompi Quartet of Duke University and alumni musicians of the Larkspur Quar
 tet in a performance of Mendelssohn's exhilarating Octet for Strings\; a 
 youthful masterpiece brimming with irrepressible energy.\n\nA reception h
 onoring Dr. Todd will follow in the Mary Duke Biddle Music Building. Plea
 se RSVP using the link on this page.\n\nFree and open to the public. All 
 are welcome!
DURATION:PT1H30M
