DESCRIPTION:Duke Chapel's carillonneurs\, Aaron Colston and Mitchell Eithu
 n\, offer this recital on the Chapel's bells. Bring a chair or blanket an
 d listen from the lawn on the Duke Chapel Quad\, or anywhere nearby.\n\nF
 ree admission. Parking is available on a first-come-first-served basis in
  the Bryan Center garage at 125 Science Drive. ADA parking is available i
 n the Bryan Center Surface Lot at the same address.\n\nThis outdoor conce
 rt is part of the J. Samuel Hammond Carillon Recital Series. Duke Chapel'
 s fifty-bell carillon is among the oldest and largest such instruments in
  the American South. Both the instrument and the recital series are named
  in honor of the late J. Samuel Hammond (1947-2021)\, University Carillon
 neur Emeritus\, who played Duke's carillon from 1964 until his retirement
  in 2018.\n\nThis recital is presented rain or shine\, and will also be l
 ivestreamed.
DURATION:PT1H
