CREATED:20260807T172344Z
DESCRIPTION:There are many federal and private funders who require data ma
 nagement (and sharing) plans as part of a grant application. NIH implemen
 ted a new Data Management and Sharing Policy in early 2023 and other fund
 ing agencies\, such as NSF\, are implementing revised public access and d
 ata sharing policies in early 2025 to comply with the "Nelson Memo" and t
 he Gold Standard of Science. This workshop will cover the components of a
  data management and sharing plan\, what makes a strong plan and how to a
 dhere to it\, and where to find guidance\, tools\, resources\, and assist
 ance for building funder-based plans. We will also discuss how to make da
 ta management plans actionable and meaningful living documents to support
  research integrity\, reproducibility\, reuse\, and verification of resul
 ts. This workshop is a collaboration of Duke University Libraries\, the O
 ffice of Scientific Integrity\, and the Medical Center Libraries and Arch
 ives. This event is open to non-Duke participants. This workshop is eligi
 ble for 2 hours of Graduate School RCR Credit (GS714) and 200-level facul
 ty and staff RCR.
DURATION:PT2H
DTSTAMP:20260807T172344Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260921T143000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260807T172344Z
